{"parentUuid":"5dfcbf29-f389-4ec5-a329-1c3a1a0fe2b6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- adopt\n- architecture-decision: Creates an Architecture Decision Record (ADR) documenting a significant technical decision, its context, alternatives considered, and consequences. Every major technical choice should have an ADR.\n- architecture-review\n- art-bible\n- asset-audit\n- asset-spec\n- autoplan\n- balance-check\n- benchmark\n- benchmark-models\n- brainstorm: Guided game concept ideation — from zero idea to a structured game concept document. Uses professional studio ideation techniques, player psychology frameworks, and structured creative exploration.\n- browse\n- bug-report\n- bug-triage\n- canary\n- careful\n- changelog\n- code-review\n- codex\n- connect-chrome\n- consistency-check\n- content-audit\n- context-restore\n- context-save\n- create-architecture\n- create-control-manifest\n- create-epics\n- create-stories\n- cso\n- day-one-patch\n- design-consultation\n- design-html\n- design-review\n- design-shotgun\n- design-system\n- dev-story\n- devex-review\n- document-generate\n- document-release\n- estimate\n- freeze\n- gate-check\n- gstack\n- gstack-upgrade\n- guard\n- health\n- help\n- hotfix\n- investigate\n- land-and-deploy\n- landing-report\n- launch-checklist\n- learn\n- localize\n- make-pdf\n- map-systems\n- milestone-review\n- office-hours\n- onboard\n- open-gstack-browser\n- pair-agent\n- patch-notes\n- perf-profile\n- plan-ceo-review\n- plan-design-review\n- plan-devex-review\n- plan-eng-review\n- plan-tune\n- playtest-report\n- project-stage-detect\n- propagate-design-change\n- prototype\n- qa\n- qa-only\n- qa-plan\n- quick-design\n- regression-suite\n- release-checklist\n- retro\n- retrospective\n- reverse-document\n- review\n- review-all-gdds\n- scope-check\n- scrape\n- security-audit\n- setup-browser-cookies\n- setup-deploy\n- setup-engine: Configure the project's game engine and version. Pins the engine in CLAUDE.md, detects knowledge gaps, and populates engine reference docs via WebSearch when the version is beyond the LLM's training data.\n- setup-gbrain\n- ship\n- skill-improve\n- skill-test\n- skillify\n- smoke-check\n- soak-test\n- sprint-plan\n- sprint-status\n- start: First-time onboarding — asks where you are, then guides you to the right workflow. No assumptions.\n- story-done\n- story-readiness\n- sync-gbrain\n- team-audio\n- team-combat\n- team-level\n- team-live-ops\n- team-narrative\n- team-polish\n- team-qa\n- team-release\n- team-ui\n- tech-debt\n- test-evidence-review\n- test-flakiness\n- test-helpers\n- test-setup\n- unfreeze\n- ux-design\n- ux-review\n- vertical-slice\n- superpowers:dispatching-parallel-agents\n- superpowers:receiving-code-review\n- superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch\n- superpowers:executing-plans\n- superpowers:brainstorming\n- superpowers:requesting-code-review\n- superpowers:using-superpowers\n- superpowers:test-driven-development\n- superpowers:using-git-worktrees\n- superpowers:verification-before-completion\n- superpowers:subagent-driven-development: Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session\n- superpowers:systematic-debugging\n- superpowers:writing-plans: Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code\n- superpowers:writing-skills\n- academic-writing-skills:academic-writing-skills\n- research-workspace:literature-triage-matrix\n- research-workspace:paper-memory-builder\n- research-workspace:research-design-helper\n- research-workspace:research-hub-multi-ai\n- research-workspace:paper-summarize\n- research-workspace:notebooklm-brief-verifier\n- research-workspace:zotero-library-curator\n- research-workspace:research-project-orienter\n- research-workspace:research-context-compressor\n- research-workspace:zotero-skills\n- research-workspace:research-hub\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \"rebind ctrl+s\", \"add a chord shortcut\", \"change the submit key\", \"customize keybindings\".\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo, defaults to 10m) - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep running /babysit-prs\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\n- claude-api: Build, debug, and optimize Claude API / Anthropic SDK apps. Apps built with this skill should include prompt caching. Also handles migrating existing Claude API code between Claude model versions (4.5 → 4.6, 4.6 → 4.7, retired-model replacements).\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for the Claude API, Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature (caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku) in a file; questions about prompt caching / cache hit rate in an Anthropic SDK project.\nSKIP: file imports `openai`/other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`/`*-generic.py`, provider-neutral code, general programming/ML.\n- init\n- review\n- security-review","skillCount":155,"isInitial":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1f19dad1-aaa0-47ee-b540-e3190368909b","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:20:27.642Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\13751","sessionId":"7ad04b1c-b250-4929-92e2-5d7da59611e9","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
