{"parentUuid":"928c181b-3620-4b17-a640-e1767ba64582","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"c78eb16c-bef9-4c73-b793-0e415b737d65","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user says HDR is off, so let me dig deeper. The symptom of \"click and it becomes normal for 1 second, then white again\" is very specific. Let me think about what else could cause this:\n\n1. Maybe Windows HDR is off but there's some other color management issue\n2. Maybe the monitor itself has HDR or some display enhancement\n3. Maybe it's a GPU driver issue with the encoder (AMF h264)\n4. Maybe it's the game-specific issue - the game might be running in HDR even though Windows HDR is off\n5. Let me check Windows HDR setting directly if possible, and also look at the monitor capture vs game capture behavior\n\nLet me read more OBS config files - maybe there's something in the encoder settings or Windows-level settings I can check.\n\nLet me also check:\n- The record encoder settings\n- Any Windows display/HDR registry settings\n- The GPU settings\n\nThe encoder being used is `h264_texture_amf` (AMD AMF encoder). This could have its own color space handling issues.\n\nAlso, when using `game_capture` with `any_fullscreen` mode, there could be issues with how it captures HDR games.\n\nLet me check Windows HDR/display settings via registry or PowerShell, and also re-examine the OBS settings more carefully.","signature":"c78eb16c-bef9-4c73-b793-0e415b737d65"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":514,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":46208,"output_tokens":644,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3a5c26a9-9d25-4ad8-8956-c78b566d64ca","timestamp":"20