{"parentUuid":"4083b9d5-5215-4cd2-927f-c2024531ac30","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"07a000a0-b9b3-4b55-ae8d-9c78dd179607","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_G2fyNbmnwPup69K11HIj7884","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ASUS AUS2581 monitor model DisplayTransferCharacteristic 120\"\n\nNo links found.\n\nThe initial search returned no results. Let me broaden the search to find more about this monitor model.\n\nNo links found.\n\nNo links found.\n\nStill no results. Let me try to identify what \"AUS2581\" refers to — it may be an EDID identifier or a different naming convention.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1Re411C7xW/?spm_id_from=333.788.recommend_more_video.17\"}]\n\nNo links found.\n\nFound it! \"AUS2581\" is the EDID identifier for the **ASUS VG258QM** — a 24.5-inch gaming monitor (also known as the TUF Gaming VG258QM). Let me search for more specific details about its EDID transfer characteristic.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"华硕 战杀25 TN\",\"url\":\"https://www.asus.com.cn/displays-desktops/monitors/tuf-gaming/tuf-gaming-vg258qm/techspec/\"},{\"title\":\"TUF Gaming VG258QM\",\"url\":\"https://www.asus.com/ch-en/displays-desktops/monitors/tuf-gaming/tuf-gaming-vg258qm/techspec/\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EDID学习\",\"url\":\"https://blog.csdn.net/u011085734/article/details/52510951\"},{\"title\":\"libdisplay-info\",\"url\":\"https://chromium.journaldev.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info/+/5d2af9a8821eca96e3e2043b9c8b7873d2152960\"},{\"title\":\"Struct DisplayGamma Copy item path\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/display-types/0.2.2/display_types/color/struct.DisplayGamma.html\"},{\"title\":\"sRGB piece-wise EOTF vs pure gamma\",\"url\":\"https://community.acescentral.com/t/srgb-piece-wise-eotf-vs-pure-gamma/4024/114\"},{\"title\":\"EDID 解读\",\"url\":\"https://blog.csdn.net/wangpeiyao5566/article/details/45269379\"},{\"title\":\"IRC Logs of #wayland on irc.freenode.net for 2023-07-10\",\"url\":\"https://people.freedesktop.org/~cbrill/dri-log/?channel=wayland&date=2023-07-10\"},{\"title\":\"HDMI EDID解读\",\"url\":\"http://www.51hei.com/bbs/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=43158&page=1#pid764526\"}]\n\n## Results\n\n### Identification of AUS2581\n\n**AUS2581** is the EDID (Extended Display Identification Data) identifier for the **ASUS TUF Gaming VG258QM** monitor. In the EDID structure:\n- `AUS` = the 3-letter manufacturer code for **ASUS**\n- `2581` = the product code assigned to the **VG258QM** model\n\nThis is a **24.5-inch TN-panel gaming monitor** with a 1920×1080 resolution and up to **280Hz refresh rate**, featuring ELMB (Extreme Low Motion Blur), Adaptive-Sync, and HDR support.\n\n### DisplayTransferCharacteristic = 120 Explained\n\nIn the EDID base block, **byte 0x17** stores the **Display Transfer Characteristic (Gamma)**. The encoding formula is:\n\n> **Stored Value = (Gamma × 100) – 100**\n\nSo for a stored value of **120**:\n\n```\n120 = (Gamma × 100) − 100\nGamma = (120 + 100) / 100 = 2.20\n```\n\nThis means the ASUS VG258QM reports a display gamma of **2.20** (often written as 2.2), which is the **standard sRGB gamma curve**. This is by far the most common gamma value reported in PC monitors — according to the [linuxhw/EDID database](https://github.com/linuxhw/EDID), over 96,000 samples report gamma 2.2, while fewer than 2,500 samples report any other value.\n\n### Key Takeaways\n\n| EDID Field | Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Manufacturer ID | `AUS` | ASUS (compressed 3-letter code) |\n| Product Code | `2581` | VG258QM model |\n| Display Transfer Characteristic | `120` | Gamma 2.20 (sRGB standard) |\n| Gamma Formula | `(120 + 100) / 100` | = 2.20 |\n\n> **Note:** The value `0xFF` (255) would indicate that gamma is undefined or specified elsewhere in an extension block. A value of 120 is the standard encoding for gamma 2.2 across virtually all consumer PC monitors.\n\n\nREMINDER: 