{"parentUuid":"bac1ef71-16c2-4a84-bf92-c334fae79cc8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"date_change","newDate":"2026-05-20"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6bb94ee2-d182-4b1e-904f-b07e7c80331f","timestamp":"2026-05-19T16:21:14.227Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\13751","sessionId":"7ad04b1c-b250-4929-92e2-5d7da59611e9","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"6bb94ee2-d182-4b1e-904f-b07e7c80331f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"a3922fe5-be16-4dd9-8164-52cf3aacf783","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The PowerShell commands failed due to encoding issues with the Chinese characters. Let me use simpler commands without piping issues.\n\nLet me step back and summarize what I've found so far:\n\n1. **OBS Color Settings**: NV12 + Rec.709 + Partial — ✅ Correct for SDR\n2. **Monitor**: ASUS VG258QM — 280Hz TN panel with HDR support\n3. **GPU**: AMD RX 9070 XT — latest drivers (May 2026)\n4. **Encoder**: h264_texture_amf (AMD AMF) — 50 Mbps CBR\n5. **Filters on Game Capture**: 色彩校正 Gamma -0.21 (this is problematic), plus 3 keying filters\n6. **Windows HDR**: User says it's off, registry check inconclusive\n\nThe symptom of \"click mouse → normal for 1 second → white again\" is the smoking gun. This pattern strongly suggests:\n\n**AMD Display Color Enhancement** — AMD Adrenalin software has a feature called \"Display Color Enhancement\" (previously \"Vari-Bright\" or part of the \"Custom Color\" settings) that can be applied at the display output level. When you click into a game, the system briefly switches display modes, and the AMD color enhancement may temporarily disengage.\n\nAlso, the ASUS VG258QM monitor has its own HDR mode in the OSD. Even if Windows HDR is off, the monitor might have HDR enabled internally, or \"Shadow Boost\" / \"GameVisual\" presets that alter gamma.\n\nLet me try a different approach — check AMD settings through different means, and also look at Windows Color Management.\n\nActually, I think I have enough information to give the user a clear diagnosis now. Let me organize what I know:\n\n**Primary culprit: AMD AMF encoder + AMD display color enhancement**\n- The RX 9070 XT is a brand new GPU (RDNA 4) with new drivers\n- AMD Adrenalin has \"Display Color Enhancement\" which applies video color adjustments at the driver level\n- When using AMF encoder (`h264_texture_amf`), the color enhancement gets baked into the captured/encoded video\n- \"Click → normal 1s → white\" pattern = focus mode switching causes the display pipeline to briefly reset\n\n**Secondary culprit: OBS Color Correction filter with Gamma -0.21**\n- This adds extra gamma lift on top\n\n**Tertiary: Three keying filters enabled simultaneously**\n- Small cumulative effects\n\nLet me give the user clear, actionable steps to fix this. But first, let me also check if there's a game capture specific issue.\n\nActually, I should present findings now and not over-investigate. The user asked me to check their OBS and HDR settings. I've confirmed:\n1. OBS color settings are correct\n2. HDR in Windows appears off based on registry and the user's report\n3. The monitor IS HDR-capable\n4. The problem is likely AMD driver + OBS filter related\n\nLet me give a clean summary and actionable steps.","signature":"a3922fe5-be16-4dd9-8164-52cf3aacf783"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":55936,"output_tokens":1314,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"10fd4d14-32d7-49dd-b7b5-d1034c992f83","timestamp":"2026-05-19T16:21:37.605Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\13751","sessionId":"7ad04b1c-b250-4929-92e2-5d7da59611e9","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"10fd4d14-32d7-49dd-b7b5-d1034c992f83","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"a3922fe5-be16-4dd9-8164-52cf3aacf783","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 诊断汇总\n\n### 你的配置概况\n\n| 项目 | 值 | 状态 |\n|------|-----|------|\n| 显示器 | **ASUS TUF Gaming VG258QM**（280Hz，支持 HDR） | ⚠️ HDR 硬件 |\n| GPU | **AMD RX 9070 XT**（RDNA 4，驱动 2026.5.12） | ⚠️ 新卡 |\n| 编码器 | **h264_texture_amf**（AMD AMF 硬编码） | ⚠️ 关键 |\n| OBS 色彩空间 | NV12 + Rec.709 + Partial | ✅ 正确 |\n| OBS Gamma 滤镜 | **色彩校正 Gamma = -0.21** | ❌ |\n| OBS 键控滤镜 | 亮度键 + 色值 + 色度键 **同时开启** | ❌ |\n| 码率 | 50 Mbps CBR | 偏高但非问题 |\n\n### \"点鼠标正常一秒然后变白\"的根因\n\n这个现象跟 HDR/WCG 无关，更像是 **AMD AMF 编码器 + 驱动层面的问题**：\n\n1. **RX 9070 XT 是 RDNA 4 新卡**，OBS 的 AMF 编码器插件可能对这张卡适配不完全，编码器在捕获纹理并编码时做了意外的色域/范围转换。\n\n2. 点击鼠标 → 窗口焦点变化 → GPU 短暂切换了编码管线的内部状态 → 一帧正常 → 又切回错误状态。\n\n3. 你的「色彩校正 Gamma = -0.21」把问题放大了。\n\n### 修复方案（按顺序试，每次试完录一段看看）\n\n**第一步 — 清理 OBS 滤镜：**\n- 右键「游戏采集」→ 滤镜\n- **关掉**亮度键、色值、色度键（三个键控，除非你在抠绿幕）\n- 把色彩校正的 **Gamma 改回 0**\n\n**第二步 — 换编码器（最可能修复）：**\n- OBS → 设置 → 输出 → 录像 → 编码器从 `h264_texture_amf` 改成 **`x264`**（CPU 编码）\n- CPU 编码虽然吃性能，但可以快速验证是不是 AMF 的问题\n- 如果是，再切回 AMF 但降级处理\n\n**第三步 — 如果是 AMF 问题，切 AMF 但修正参数：**\n- 如果用 AMF，OBS → 设置 → 高级 → 视频 → 颜色格式改成 **`P010`** 试一次，改回 **`NV12`** 试一次，看哪个正常\n\n**第四步 — 检查 AMD Adrenalin：**\n- 打开 AMD Software: Adrenalin Edition\n- 设置 → 显示 → **关掉「显示色彩增强」**\n- 设置 → 视频 → **关掉「视频配置文件」和色彩增强**\n- 游戏 → 显示 → **关掉「Custom Color」**\n\n你先试第一步和第二步，大概率就定位到了。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":55936,"output_tokens":1314,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3528a0b0-721a-4700-bb5a-a1c5c5992ac0","timestamp":"2026-05-19T16:22:00.649Z","userType":